# REM-001 — Reconcile current authority and publish the remediation RAG

## Objective

Create the truthful authority baseline required before the rest of the remediation programme executes.

This is a **documentation/tracker/authority reconciliation** issue. It must not silently implement player physics, barrel physics, Water semantics, Stage-3B discovery, or unrelated cleanup.

At programme creation the audited `main` is `e87ac54459a3a62350fa7aa3da6ce979c30a18b8`, but **do not assume that SHA is still authoritative when execution begins**.

## Why this work exists

The 2026-09-20 audit found that current and historical records conflate:

- code implemented on a branch;
- code actually integrated into current main;
- evidence passing for a bounded fixture/platform;
- acceptance of the intended gameplay/product behaviour.

The same flattening left #8 with stale parent logic, #10/#11 administratively completed despite later owner rejection of the broad behavioural outcome, and current programme summaries lagging later development.

This issue creates the canonical RAG authority that all later REM work uses.

## Required RAG / authority reading

Before editing, read in full:

- root `AGENTS.md`;
- #79 and every finding/disposition in its table;
- #8, #9, #10, #11, #12, #14, #18, #19, #20, #26, #30, #45, #49, #56–#70;
- `docs/reference/status-and-roadmap.md`;
- `docs/reference/validation-evidence.md`;
- `docs/reference/retrieval-index.md` and `retrieval-corpus.json`;
- `docs/operations/cybersand-codex-development-handover.md`;
- `docs/operations/documentation-maintenance.md`;
- `docs/operations/architecture-programme.md`;
- `docs/operations/microscenarios-programme.md`;
- `docs/operations/soliding-programme.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-09-issue-10-granular-policy.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-13-issue-11-repair.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-12-issue-19-water-feel-lab.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-19-issue-26-post-merge-review.md`;
- the source paths needed only to distinguish current truth from historical claims.

## Required repository outputs

Publish two focused Markdown documents:

### 1. Immutable dated audit

`docs/audits/2026-09-20-development-claims-closure-audit.md`

It must retain the nineteen F01–F19 findings, their classification, evidence boundaries, corrected historical incidents, and explicit coverage limitations. It must not claim that a fresh physics campaign was run if none was run.

### 2. Canonical remediation programme

`docs/operations/development-claims-remediation-programme.md`

It must own:

- the F01–F19 mapping;
- REM dependency graph;
- implementation/integration/verification/acceptance distinctions;
- existing #49 ownership rather than a duplicate Water apparatus issue;
- concurrency rules with #12 Stage-3B;
- child exit criteria;
- final REM-008 certification gate.

Route this page through the normal RAG hierarchy: docs navigation, roadmap/handover and retrieval routes as appropriate. Keep the hierarchy focused; do not duplicate subsystem contracts into one giant page.

## Tracker reconciliation

Re-read live issue state before changing anything.

### #8

Keep #8 open. Add/reconcile current parent text so it no longer says or implies that #10/#11 broad product behaviour is accepted or that #8 merely waits on the old bounded #12 route.

It must distinguish:

- #9 characterization: retained valid scoped evidence;
- #10: bounded policy/fixture implementation evidence retained, broader player/granular gameplay acceptance open;
- #11: bounded historical repair evidence retained, current-main integration identity handled by REM-002, broader body/granular gameplay acceptance open;
- #12: independently promoted soliding programme, not the sole remaining reason #8 is open.

### #10 / #11

Do **not** erase historical completion comments or rewrite their evidence.

Reconcile their current status in the least misleading repository-native way after inspecting current GitHub state. The governing meaning must be:

> Prior work remains accepted as a bounded first-stage result within its tested envelope. Subsequent owner evaluation finds the overall gameplay behaviour materially below acceptable quality; the broader behavioural objective therefore remains open.

If reopening #10/#11 is the clearest repository-native representation, do so and record why. If a current repository mechanism makes another representation clearly superior, document the reasoning and ensure no duplicate ownership is created. Do not invent a new successor merely to preserve a misleading completed state.

### Parent/programme summaries

Repair stale present-tense routing in current canonical docs and issue bodies where it materially misstates the current stage. Preserve dated historical sections as history.

In particular reconcile F19-type stale summaries in #12/#30/roadmap/handover without rewriting the original historical decision records.

## Explicit non-scope

- no player/granular implementation;
- no body/granular implementation;
- no port/cherry-pick of #11 code;
- no Water solver or #49 implementation;
- no H-capture implementation;
- no Stage-3B implementation;
- no CI runner redesign;
- no mass issue closing/reopening merely for visual tidiness.

## Full execution prompt

Execute this issue autonomously from current authoritative main.

1. Inspect repo/root/HEAD/status/remotes/open work and verify there is no existing REM-001 owner/branch/PR.
2. Reconcile any changes since the programme creation SHA.
3. Read the authority set above in full.
4. Produce the dated audit and canonical remediation programme.
5. Reconcile #8/#10/#11 and stale current programme routing according to the rules above; preserve all historical evidence.
6. Update docs navigation, RAG retrieval manifest/questions only as needed for reliable retrieval of the new canonical programme.
7. Run the complete documentation/repository/history/retrieval gates required by `AGENTS.md`.
8. Review the final diff for accidental implementation changes or historical rewrites.
9. Open a focused PR that references #79 and this issue.
10. After required automated checks pass, merge the PR if the repository's normal authority allows it; otherwise leave it review-ready and record the precise remaining gate.
11. Verify the landed exact main head before closing this issue.
12. Update #79 with the landed RAG path and exact completion identity.

## Acceptance

- [ ] F01–F19 have durable repository routing.
- [ ] The canonical remediation RAG exists and is retrievable.
- [ ] #8 is visibly open for the correct current reasons.
- [ ] #10/#11 bounded evidence is preserved but no longer masquerades as broad owner acceptance.
- [ ] Historical #12/MS-001/#26 corrections remain historical and are not rewritten as if they never happened.
- [ ] Current programme summaries match live dependency state.
- [ ] No simulation/runtime semantics changed.
- [ ] Documentation, repository, history and retrieval gates pass or explicit inherited failures are reported without being relabelled.
- [ ] Exact landed commit is recorded.

Completion of REM-001 unblocks REM-002, REM-003, REM-005, REM-006, REM-007 and the already-existing #49 remediation lane.

## Owner / hybrid clarification — 2026-09-20

This issue remains F01 forensic/remediation work, but its implementation interpretation is narrowed by later owner clarification:

- the "barrel" is only a generic rectangular Rapier reference body;
- the owner does **not** recall accepting the historical #11 support result as final body behavior;
- preserve the historical bounded evidence exactly, but do not infer owner acceptance from the old record's wording;
- do not create a barrel-specific support/contact owner;
- read #90 and `docs/operations/water-hybrid-pressure-extension-programme.md`, especially #91/#92, plus the live #12 soliding/hybrid authority before source changes;
- current Stage 3B discovery is not itself the later dynamic cell↔Rapier substrate;
- if an active generic hybrid implementation owns the same coupling semantics/write set, complete the forensic classification but stop before creating a competing implementation. Coordinate, adapt, or explicitly defer the semantic repair into the generic owner with a retrievable disposition.

The objective is truthful provenance plus the still-valid **generic** coupling contract, not restoration of historical code for its own sake.

