# REM-002 — Reconstruct #11 integration history and reconcile bounded generic body↔granular semantics

## Objective

Determine exactly why the historical bounded #11 body↔granular repair/evidence checkpoint is not the coupling implementation on audited main, classify the divergence without guessing, and reconcile the still-valid **generic body↔cellular** semantics with current authoritative main.

This issue resolves **F01**. It does **not** claim that the historical #11 repair is sufficient for acceptable body↔granular gameplay; that broader acceptance belongs to REM-004.

## Canonical RAG / required reading

After #80 lands, read and treat as governing programme authority:

- `docs/operations/development-claims-remediation-programme.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-20-development-claims-closure-audit.md`.

Also read in full:

- root `AGENTS.md`;
- #8, #10, #11, #12 and #79/#80;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-13-issue-11-repair.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-12-issue-11-reconciliation.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-09-physics-characterisation.md`;
- `docs/audits/2026-09-09-issue-10-granular-policy.md`;
- `docs/architecture/rigid-body-and-cellular-coupling.md`;
- `docs/systems/granular-interaction-policy.md`;
- current roadmap/handover/validation evidence;
- current #12/Stage-3B production authority wherever write-set or ownership overlap is possible.

Historical evidence identities include #11 repair commit `f8720d331e653ff40c12149dc1b7164724accd9f` and evidence record commit `d5f0de687283ec366ed4ff33160a274e2a35ddc6`. Treat those as **historical evidence identities**, not as an instruction to cherry-pick them blindly.

## Audit finding to resolve

The historical #11 bounded record says that checkpoint provided, among other things:

- masked-source feedback correction;
- barrier-/foreign-mask-aware bounded ejection;
- current-cell granular bearing;
- excavation removing support;
- an ordinary rectangle/load acceptance envelope.

The audited main `e87ac54459a3a62350fa7aa3da6ce979c30a18b8` instead showed an older endpoint-only ejection path and lacked the accepted bearing contribution in the inspected result path.

The unresolved question is **how that divergence happened and what the current correct implementation should be**.

## Required forensic phase

Before changing source:

1. Verify current main, issue/PR/branch ownership and whether any later work has already resolved all or part of this.
2. Reconstruct the ancestry/integration path from the accepted #11 branch/evidence to current main.
3. Produce a symbol/file provenance matrix for at least:
   - `prepare_rigid_body_coupling` and body-state parsing;
   - overlap reconciliation;
   - ejection target/path validation;
   - masked-source behavior;
   - granular support/bearing accumulation;
   - result/correction/impulse ABI;
   - body diagnostics;
   - relevant native/Godot/browser tests;
   - coupling documentation and runtime provenance.
4. Classify every historical bounded #11 change as:
