### 2. Sealed/recoverable study identity

The system must preserve enough hidden information to reconstruct the experiment even after a crash, but normal observer operation must not reveal it.

Use a durable, explicit mechanism consistent with repository capabilities. Do not claim cryptographic secrecy if the mechanism is only accidental/base64/obscured storage.

### 3. Post-observation reveal

An explicit finish/reveal action may produce the full candidate mapping and join it to the retained observations after the observer has completed the blind record.

