Do not silently reuse or overwrite an existing non-empty formal-H session.

The formal path must be able to demonstrate that every recorded observation belongs to the world/policy application that was actually acknowledged before capture.

## Apply/reset synchronization

A candidate change must not be capturable while the worker/world still represents the previous candidate.

Required flow:

1. request candidate;
2. validate candidate;
3. apply through existing legal reset/owner boundary;
4. wait for explicit effective-policy/world acknowledgement;
5. enable capture;
6. record observation;
7. only then allow next candidate/reset as defined by the protocol.

